","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"standard"},{"text":": The legacy hillshade method.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"basic"},{"text":": Basic hillshade. Uses a simple physics model where the reflected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light intensity is proportional to the cosine of the angle between the incident","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"light and the surface normal. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" default algorithm.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"combined","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Hillshade algorithm whose intensity scales with slope. Similar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gdaldem"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-combined"},{"text":" option.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"igor"},{"text":": Hillshade algorithm which tries to minimize effects on other map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"features beneath. Similar to GDAL’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"gdaldem","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-igor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" option.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"multidirectional"},{"type":"text","text":": Hillshade with multiple illumination directions. Uses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the basic hillshade model with multiple independent light sources.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Predefined functions, including mathematical and string operators"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Conditional expressions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Variable assignments and references to assigned variables","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Step functions a